<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <VersionPrefix>1.5.71-beta1</VersionPrefix>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>* Align with **Akka.NET 1.5.71**; upgrade to **Quartz 4.0.1** and target **.NET 10 only**. This drops .NET Standard/.NET Framework and older .NET support despite retaining aligned 1.5 package numbering. Users who cannot move to .NET 10 should pin Akka.Quartz.Actor **1.5.59**.
* **Read the [upgrade guide](https://github.com/akkadotnet/Akka.Quartz.Actor/blob/dev/docs/upgrading-to-quartz4.md) before upgrading** ([local copy](docs/upgrading-to-quartz4.md)). It is also included in the NuGet package and the separate upgrade-helper archive.
* Existing ADO stores require the [official Quartz 4.0.1 schema upgrade script](https://github.com/quartznet/quartznet/tree/v4.0.1/database/migrations/4.0), a cron audit and an offline cutover. Never use the destructive fresh-install `tables_&lt;db&gt;.sql` scripts. Quartz **4.0.1 rejects** textual weekday steps such as `MON/2`; select replacements deliberately.
* Added separate .NET 8 / Quartz 3 binary-to-Newtonsoft converter and .NET 10 / Quartz 4 read-only auditor for **SQL Server, PostgreSQL and SQLite**. Conversion defaults to dry-run, requires explicit trust and stopped-scheduler acknowledgements to apply, preserves schedule columns, and rolls back on failure. Custom BLOB triggers require application-specific migration. Neither helper starts a scheduler or applies schema changes.
* Legacy Akka message `byte[]` values inside compatible Newtonsoft JSON remain readable. This does **not** make BinaryFormatter-backed database blobs readable: convert those before leaving Quartz 3. Newly saved messages use Base64 strings, so mixed old/new writers and application-only rollback are unsafe; see the upgrade guide.
* Replace `Quartz.Serialization.Json` with `Quartz.Serialization.Newtonsoft`, explicitly keep `quartz.serializer.type=newtonsoft` for existing Newtonsoft stores, and update direct Quartz packages/APIs together. `IJob.Execute` returns `ValueTask` and receives a `CancellationToken`; see the [pinned upstream migration guide](https://github.com/quartznet/quartznet/blob/v4.0.1/docs/documentation/quartz-4.x/migration-guide.md).
* Quartz 4 removed the process-wide scheduler registry. Identical scheduler names no longer share a RAM scheduler; explicitly supply a shared scheduler where needed.
* Install persistent actor context **before** starting an actor-owned scheduler. `OnSchedulerCreated` overrides now run before startup. Documented readiness ordering for caller-owned schedulers; actor-owned schedulers now dispose independently of a stopped actor mailbox.
* Invalid job requests return one failure and create no job. Added real SQL Server/PostgreSQL container conversion and delivery checks, plus SQLite binary-conversion, rollback, restart, misfire, failed-write, schema and audit regressions and scheduler lifecycle checks.
* Run all `*Tests.csproj` projects in CI, fail immediately on each test process failure and require fresh reports with executed tests. Test projects use xunit.v3 / Microsoft.Testing.Platform.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>